For the purposes of writing a single NMState capture-based config that will work in most scenarios, we would like to have configuration for both static and DHCP addressing in the same config. Unfortunately, this is a problem today because the capture data does not include certain fields if they don’t apply to the running config. For example, in a static IP cluster, the following config does not work:

{noformat}    capture:
      base-iface: interfaces.alt-names.0.name == "primary"
      base-iface-routes: routes.running.next-hop-interface==capture.base-iface.interfaces.0.name
      bridge-routes: capture.base-iface-routes | routes.running.next-hop-interface:="br-ex"
    desiredState:
      interfaces:
...
      - name: br-ex
        type: ovs-interface
        state: up
        copy-mac-from: {{`"{{ capture.base-iface.interfaces.0.name }}"`}}
        mtu: {{`"{{ capture.base-iface.interfaces.0.mtu }}"`}}
        wait-ip: {{`"{{ capture.base-iface.interfaces.0.wait-ip }}"`}}
        ipv4:
          enabled: {{`"{{ capture.base-iface.interfaces.0.ipv4.enabled }}"`}}
          dhcp: {{`"{{ capture.base-iface.interfaces.0.ipv4.dhcp }}"`}}
          address: {{`"{{ capture.base-iface.interfaces.0.ipv4.address }}"`}}
          auto-route-metric: 48
          # FIXME: Not present for static.
          auto-dns: {{`"{{ capture.base-iface.interfaces.0.ipv4.auto-dns }}"`}}
          auto-gateway: {{`"{{ capture.base-iface.interfaces.0.ipv4.auto-gateway }}"`}}
          auto-routes: {{`"{{ capture.base-iface.interfaces.0.ipv4.auto-routes }}"`}}{noformat}

The auto-* fields aren’t present in the capture data, so this configuration fails. There are a couple of options for addressing this:

# Include the value for all fields, even ones that aren’t explicitly set. In a static IP configuration, auto-dns presumably defaults to false.
# Provide a way to set a fallback value for the field if it’s missing from the capture data.

